<title>POLAND: Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</title>
<headline>Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish T-bills fell at Monday's primary auction on total demand of 750 million zlotys against a 1.1 billion zlotys offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry sold bills worth 585 million zlotys.</p>
<p>The ministry will offer 1.1 billion zlotys worth of bills at its next primary auction on Monday, August 4.  </p>
<p>			 8-week   13-week  26-week  52-week</p>
<p> new min price     96.70    94.75    89.91    81.60</p>
<p> (pvs auction)    (96.72)  (94.78)  (89.95)  (81.67)</p>
<p> new max price     96.77    94.90    90.08    81.80</p>
<p> (pvs auction)    (97.27)  (94.95)  (90.10)  (81.82)</p>
<p> offer		200.00   200.00   200.00   500.00</p>
<p> bids recorded    241.14   265.12    48.19   195.14</p>
<p> bids accepted    181.72   209.74    37.39   155.84</p>
<p> next auction     200.00   200.00   200.00   500.00</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
